  "round_4": "W1 and W2 stand 0.4 m toward the kerb from the pavement's middle (x -3.7 and 3.7): the nearest house front fills less of the frame's side and the lane head's corner shows. W3's eye is 5.6 m above the lane (the end terrace on a raised footway 1 m up), so the queue's tail, 6 m in front of W1's composed spot, reaches about 0.70 down in W3. No. 1's brazier stands against the outer pier with the stooped man at its front-left, the PETROL and DIESEL drums to its right with both words whole from W1; the queue stands along the kerb to the right of them, 1.1 m apart. No. 2's drums stand by its outer pier with a clear gap, both words whole from W2. The handcart is on the right pavement in W3's bottom third. No. 1's yard is in a faint cool light (its gate's bars show against it); a warm beam from No. 2's yard lies along the pavement in W2; one curtained window glows on each gate view's quiet side."
